<audio id="sc-audio" controls></audio>
```

```js
function playTrack(trackId) {
  // Build the streaming URL (requires a client_id)
  const streamUrl = `https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/${trackId}/stream?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID`;

  const audio = document.getElementById('sc-audio');
  audio.src = streamUrl;
  audio.play();
}
```

> **Important:**  
> * For **private** tracks you must include the OAuth `access_token` instead of the client_id:  
> `.../stream?oauth_token=USER_ACCESS_TOKEN`  
> * The streaming URL is **CORS‑enabled**, so you can control it from JavaScript without any extra proxy.

### 4.6. Building a simple playlist UI  

```js
let playlist = [];   // array of track objects
let currentIdx = 0;

function loadPlaylist(trackUrls) {
  // Resolve each URL, then store the track objects
  const promises = trackUrls.map(url => SC.resolve(url));
  Promise.all(promises).then(tracks => {
    playlist = tracks;
    currentIdx = 0;
    playCurrent();
  });
}

function playCurrent() {
  const track = playlist[currentIdx];
  if (!track) return;
  playTrack(track.id);
  document.getElementById('now-playing').textContent = `${track.title} – ${track.user.username}`;
}

// Next / Prev buttons
document.getElementById('nextBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
  currentIdx = (currentIdx + 1) % playlist.length;
  playCurrent();
});
document.getElementById('prevBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
  currentIdx = (currentIdx - 1 + playlist.length) % playlist.length;
  playCurrent();
});
```

```html
<div id="now-playing">Nothing playing</div>
<button id="prevBtn">Prev</button>
<button id="nextBtn">Next</button>
```

### 4.7. Handling playback events (progress, end, errors)

```js
const audio = document.getElementById('sc-audio');

audio.addEventListener('timeupdate', () => {
  const percent = (audio.currentTime / audio.duration) * 100;
  document.getElementById('progressBar').style.width = `${percent}%`;
});

audio.addEventListener('ended', () => {
  // Auto‑advance to next track
  document.getElementById('nextBtn').click();
});

audio.addEventListener('error', e => {
  console.error('Playback error', e);
});
```

```html
<div style="background:#eee; width:100%; height:6px; position:relative;">
  <div id="progressBar" style="background:#ff5500; width:0%; height:100%;"></div>
</div>
```

---

## 5.  Server‑Side Considerations  

| Use‑case | Why you might need a backend | What to do |
|----------|-----------------------------|------------|
| **Securely store the client secret** | The secret must never be exposed to the browser. | Keep it in an environment variable; use it only when exchanging the OAuth `code` for an access token. |
| **Cache track metadata** | Reducing API calls improves performance and avoids rate limits. | Store track objects (id, title, artwork_url, duration) in a DB or in‑memory cache (Redis, etc.). |
| **Serve a proxy for streaming** (rare) | Some browsers block cross‑origin audio streams if the `Access‑Control‑Allow-Origin` header is missing. | Use a simple proxy endpoint that forwards the stream URL with proper CORS headers. (Usually not needed; SoundCloud already sends CORS headers.) |

---

## 6.  Common Pitfalls & How to Avoid Them  

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **“401 Unauthorized” when streaming** | Using a client‑id for a private track, or token expired. | Switch to `oauth_token=USER_ACCESS_TOKEN` for private content, and refresh the token when needed. |
| **No sound on iOS Safari** | Autoplay is blocked; iOS requires a user gesture before playing audio. | Attach `audio.play()` to a click/tap event (e.g., a “Play” button). |
| **CORS error in Chrome console** | Trying to fetch the stream from a domain not whitelisted (rare). | Ensure you’re using the official `api.soundcloud.com` endpoint; no custom proxy needed. |
| **Rate‑limit errors (429)** | Too many API calls in a short period. | Implement exponential back‑off, cache results, and request only the data you need. |
| **Widget height looks wrong** | Using the `visual=true` parameter but setting a small height. | For visual mode, set height ≈ 450 px; for compact mode, 166 px works. |

---

## 7.  Full Minimal Example (Custom UI + OAuth)  

Below is a **single‑file** HTML demo that:

1. Authenticates the user (OAuth popup).  
2. Resolves three public tracks.  
3. Plays them with a custom UI (play/pause, next/prev, progress bar).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>SoundCloud Player Demo</title>
<script src="https://connect.soundcloud.com/sdk/sdk-3.3.2.js"></script>
<style>
  body {font-family:Arial, sans-serif; max-width:600px; margin:2rem auto;}
  #player {margin-top:1rem;}
  #progress {background:#eee; height:6px; position:relative;}
  #progress div {background:#ff5500; height:100%; width:0%;}
  button {margin:0.2rem;}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>My SoundCloud Player</h1>
<button id="loginBtn">Log in with SoundCloud</button>
<div id="nowPlaying">Not logged in</div>

<div id="player" style="display:none;">
  <audio id="audio" controls></audio>
  <div id="progress"><div></div></div>
  <button id="prevBtn">Prev</button>
  <button id="playPauseBtn">Play</button>
  <button id="nextBtn">Next</button>
</div>

<script>
/* ==== CONFIG ==== */
const CLIENT_ID = 'YOUR_CLIENT_ID';          // <-- replace
const REDIRECT_URI = 'https://mywebsite.com/auth/callback'; // must match app settings
/* ================= */

SC.initialize({ client_id: CLIENT_ID, redirect_uri: REDIRECT_URI });

let accessToken = null;   // will hold the OAuth token after login
let playlist = [];        // array of track objects
let currentIdx = 0;

// ---------- AUTH ----------
document.getElementById('loginBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
  SC.connect().then(session => {
    accessToken = session.access_token;
    document.getElementById('nowPlaying').textContent = `Logged in as ${session.user.username}`;
    document.getElementById('player').style.display = 'block';
    loadDemoPlaylist();
  }).catch(err => console.error('Auth error', err));
});

// ---------- PLAYLIST ----------
function loadDemoPlaylist() {
  const urls = [
    'https://soundcloud.com/artist1/track-one',
    'https://soundcloud.com/artist2/track-two',
    'https://soundcloud.com/artist3/track-three'
  ];
  Promise.all(urls.map(url => SC.resolve(url))).then(tracks => {
    playlist = tracks;
    currentIdx = 0;
    updateNowPlaying();
    setAudioSource();
  });
}

// ---------- UI & PLAYBACK ----------
const audio = document.getElementById('audio');
const playPauseBtn = document.getElementById('playPauseBtn');

function setAudioSource() {
  const track = playlist[currentIdx];
  if (!track) return;
  const streamUrl = `https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/${track.id}/stream?oauth_token=${accessToken}`;
  audio.src = streamUrl;
  audio.play();
  playPauseBtn.textContent = 'Pause';
}

function updateNowPlaying() {
  const track = playlist[currentIdx];
  document.getElementById('nowPlaying').textContent = `${track.title} – ${track.user.username}`;
}

// Controls
document.getElementById('prevBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
  currentIdx = (currentIdx - 1 + playlist.length) % playlist.length;
  setAudioSource();
  updateNowPlaying();
});

document.getElementById('nextBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
  currentIdx = (currentIdx + 1) % playlist.length;
  setAudioSource();
  updateNowPlaying();
});

playPauseBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  if (audio.paused) {
    audio.play();
    playPauseBtn.textContent = 'Pause';
  } else {
    audio.pause();
    playPauseBtn.textContent = 'Play';
  }
});

// Progress bar
audio.addEventListener('timeupdate', () => {
  const percent = (audio.currentTime / audio.duration) * 100;
  document.querySelector('#progress div').style.width = `${percent}%`;
});
audio.addEventListener('ended', () => {
  document.getElementById('nextBtn').click();
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**What to replace before using:**

* `YOUR_CLIENT_ID` → your SoundCloud client id.  
* `REDIRECT_URI` → the exact URL you set in the SoundCloud app settings.  
* The three track URLs in `loadDemoPlaylist()` → any public (or private, if you have permission) tracks you want to showcase.

---

## 8.  Next‑Level Enhancements  

| Feature | How to implement |
|---------|------------------|
| **Visual waveform** | Use the **WaveSurfer.js** library and feed it the track’s `stream_url`. |
| **Lazy‑load artwork** | Each track object contains `artwork_url`. Replace `-large` with `-t500x500` for higher‑resolution images. |
