## 4️⃣ Using the REST API (Optional)

If you need more than just playback—e.g., fetching a user’s liked tracks, uploading a new track, or reading analytics—you can call SoundCloud’s REST endpoints directly with the token:

```js
// Example: Get the authenticated user's profile
SC.get('/me').then(function(user) {
  console.log('Logged‑in user:', user);
});
```

All API calls automatically include the `oauth_token` you set during `SC.initialize`.

## 5️⃣ Refreshing the Token (When It Expires)

The token we received is short‑lived (1 hour). When it expires, you’ll need to re‑run the OAuth flow or implement a refresh‑token flow if you requested offline access. The simplest approach for a web app is to redirect the user to the authorization URL again:

```js
// Build the auth URL (you can generate it server‑side)
const authUrl = `https://soundcloud.com/connect?client_id=client321&redirect_uri=${encodeURIComponent('https://soundcloud.com/callback')}&response_type=code&scope=*`;

// Redirect the user
window.location.href = authUrl;
```

When SoundCloud redirects back to `https://soundcloud.com/callback?code=...`, exchange that `code` for a new token on your server.

